  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Nuedexta (dextromethorphan/quinidine), an NMDA-sigma / pba-agent; effective 2019-03-11. Approval and explicit denial gates encoded; documentation and therapeutic-dose failure or contraindication attestations require manual review.",
    "Source discrepancy: approval criterion 2 includes Parkinson’s disease and Alzheimer’s disease, but denial criterion 2 omits them. Both remain eligible per the approval criteria. SSRI and TCA requirements are separate; each requires therapeutic-dose failure or contraindication to use.",
    "Cautions (notes only): certain prescription and OTC medications have significant drug interactions when taken concomitantly. Thrombocytopenia, hepatitis, and other hypersensitivity reactions have occurred.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 1 year with documentation of decreased laughing or crying episodes from baseline. Manual review required.",
    "Quantity and dosing (notes only): 60 capsules/month; start 1 capsule daily for 7 days, then 1 capsule every 12 hours thereafter. No numeric quantity enforcement; manual review required."
  ],
